HZ = ('The two windows, however, differ in horizon: the normal-period outcomes lie one to two years after their baseline and the late-recovery outcomes four to six years after. '
      'The pre-specified horizon-matched check (Section 2.6) removes this difference for the four missions observed since FY2012/13. In the same eleven groups, mean masking in pre-pandemic data is 0.071 one to two years after the baseline but 0.181 four to six years after, against 0.215 in late recovery (ratio 1.19; medians 0.165 and 0.193). '
      'Under the pre-specified rule, the late-recovery contrast is therefore softened: much of the original difference reflects horizon. Two sensitivity versions give ratios of 1.19 and 1.32. '
      'The normal-period value is strongly affected by one group: the Royal Armouries\' organised on-site under-18 series falls by 96% between FY2015/16 and FY2016/17 while its visits fall by 4%, which is consistent with an undocumented reporting change; excluding it post hoc gives 0.128 against 0.233 (ratio 1.82). '
      'By contrast, the depth of shortfall differs in every version: at (τ=.90), none of the 33 horizon-matched pre-pandemic museum-years is RED and 13 are GREEN, whereas 14 late-recovery museum-years are RED and four GREEN, and mean weakest-mission attainment falls from 0.73 to 0.53 (Fig. 5B).')
